1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,840
After six hours of driving like a boss we finally arrived at our hotel in ambleside.
开了六个小时的车，像个高手一样，我们终于抵达安布尔赛德的酒店。

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:09,760
Now there is an abundance of great accommodation in the lake district.
湖区有很多很棒的住宿选择。

3
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:18,710
But we chose this one due to its reasonable price close proximity to water and central location to most of the sites we wanted to visit.
但我们选这一家，是因为价格合理、靠近水边，而且相对我们想去的大多数景点，位置很居中。

4
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:22,400
Just a short walk from our front door sat lake windermere.
从酒店门口走一小段路，就是温德米尔湖。

5
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:39,590
Stretching over 10 miles windermere is england's largest lake with ambleside marking its northernmost point.
温德米尔湖绵延十多英里，作者说它是英格兰最大的湖泊，安布尔赛德位于其最北端。

6
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:44,240
Since we arrived mid afternoon today was more about getting familiar with our local area.
因为我们下午中段才到，今天主要是熟悉周围的环境。

7
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:49,730
And after a 20 minute meander we explored ambleside's main town.
悠闲走了二十分钟后，我们逛了安布尔赛德的镇中心。

8
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:12,390
There are arguably two local foods that you have to try when in the lake district and the first was found in this sweet shop.
可以说，湖区有两种当地食物值得尝尝，第一种就在这家糖果店里。

9
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:22,790
Sitting alongside some lovely looking fudge and chocolate was kendal mint cake a peppermint flavored snack made mostly out of sugar and glucose.
在看起来很好吃的软糖和巧克力旁，摆着肯德尔薄荷糕：一种以糖和葡萄糖为主要原料的薄荷味零食。

10
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:29,269
It's considered as the original energy bar and is still popular with climbers and hikers today.
作者说，它被视为最初的能量棒，至今仍受到登山者和徒步者欢迎。

11
00:01:29,279 --> 00:01:34,790
Taste wise there's not much like it to be fair so it's definitely worth a try for the experience.
说到味道，说实话，它挺独特的，所以为体验一下也很值得尝尝。

12
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:44,310
It's very minty and even though the first bite is relatively hard the glucose dissolves quickly filling your mouth with sugary goodness.
薄荷味非常浓；虽然第一口比较硬，葡萄糖却很快化开，让嘴里充满甜味。

13
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:48,960
To set the scene for this vlog we are by no means experienced hikers.
先交代一下这趟视频的背景：我们绝对算不上经验丰富的徒步者。

14
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:53,680
So any energy boost we could get from kendal mint cake would be appreciated.
所以，肯德尔薄荷糕能给我们补充一点能量，我们都会很欢迎。

15
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:59,269
There was a very real chance that at least one of us would collapse during this trip.
这趟旅行中，我们至少有一个人累倒的可能性可不小。

16
00:01:59,279 --> 00:02:10,629
Our first full day tomorrow would be to my favorite village in the lake district and it would also mark the starting point to our first hike up a mountain.
明天是我们的第一个完整旅行日，要去的是我最喜欢的湖区村庄；它也是我们第一次登山徒步的起点。

17
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:15,040
Looking out our hotel window it seemed the weather was still on our side.
望向酒店窗外，看来天气仍然眷顾我们。

18
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:19,440
The lake district is after all the wettest part of England.
毕竟，作者说湖区是英格兰最湿润的地区。

19
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:23,400
We sat down for a full english breakfast then made our way to grasmere.
我们坐下来吃了一顿全套英式早餐，然后动身前往格拉斯米尔。

20
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:30,790
It was still early in the morning and we quickly moved past all the interesting spots as we'd return here later.
当时还很早，我们迅速经过那些有趣的地方，因为稍后还会回来。

21
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:34,870
Our immediate goal was to reach the summit of helm crag.
眼前的目标，是登上海尔姆峰的山顶。

22
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:44,629
Rising 400 meters this is a relatively popular hike so we thought it best to start here since if we did have a heart attack there would be someone nearby.
这座山高约四百米，路线相对热门；我们想先走这里比较好，万一真有心脏病发作，附近还会有人。

23
00:02:44,639 --> 00:02:51,359
Indeed one of my favorite things about being on a countryside walk is that moment where you pass another human being.
的确，乡间散步最让我喜欢的事情之一，就是和另一个人迎面走过的那一刻。

24
00:02:51,359 --> 00:02:54,639
This man here actually acknowledged my existence.
看，这个人居然注意到我的存在，还跟我打了招呼。

25
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:57,349
We certainly weren't in london anymore.
我们显然已经不在伦敦了。

26
00:02:57,359 --> 00:03:04,400
Armed with the motivation of a total stranger saying hello we carried that through our footsteps towards helm crag.
一个完全陌生的人向我们问好，就给了我们动力；我们带着这股劲，继续一步步走向海尔姆峰。
